1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:03,900
Fifty thousand people open the same celebrity profile at once.

2
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:10,820
Without a cache, every request hits the database. Connections fill, disk reads pile up, and latency grows.

3
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:17,600
The cache checks first. On a miss, read the database, store the result, then respond.

4
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:23,480
On a hit, hot data returns from memory in roughly one point one milliseconds, instead of four.

5
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:29,860
A TTL limits staleness. Caching removes repeated reads, but stampedes still need design.
